<title>UK: Deutsche Ausgleichsbank plans 1.5 bln mark bond.</title>
<headline>Deutsche Ausgleichsbank plans 1.5 bln mark bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Deutsche Ausgleichsbank plans to issue a 1.5 billion mark 10-year Euro-Asian bond this week, syndicate managers said on Monday.</p>
<p>Commerzbank and HSBC Trinkaus were tipped as joint lead managers, they said.</p>
<p>Deutsche Ausgleichsbank held presentations in Asia last week for the deal, which is expected to be listed in Asia and Europe. Spread talk was in the high-10s basis points over Bunds.</p>
<p>Deutsche Ausgleichsbank last tapped the Eurobond in February when it issued a $300 million five-year bond via Deutsche Morgan Grenfell and Merrill Lynch.</p>
<p>-- Aline van Duyn, London Newsroom +44 171 542 7748</p>
